import{_ as e,c as o,o as i,a3 as d}from"./chunks/framework.Bsyxd66g.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Config and persistence","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"subsystems/config-and-persistence.md","filePath":"subsystems/config-and-persistence.md","lastUpdated":1794660158000}'),c={name:"subsystems/config-and-persistence.md"},t=d('<h1 id="config-and-persistence" tabindex="-1">Config and persistence <a class="header-anchor" href="#config-and-persistence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Config and persistence&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="responsibility-and-boundaries" tabindex="-1">Responsibility and boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#responsibility-and-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Responsibility and boundaries&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Owns: the <code>Config</code> schema and its validation, the single-row <code>config</code> table that stores it, the in-process <code>VersionedConfig</code> singleton with optimistic version checking, the <code>VersionedCache</code> fan-out used by derived caches (<code>TEMPLATE</code>, rate limiter, <code>BiliClient</code>), the SQLite connection/migration setup on disk, and the entity/table shapes that everything else reads.</li><li>Does not own: how configuration values are used (<a href="./sync-pipeline">sync-pipeline.md</a>, <a href="./media-artifacts">media-artifacts.md</a>, <a href="./notifications">notifications.md</a>, <a href="./web-ui">web-ui.md</a>); HTTP routes that expose config (<a href="./web-api-server">web-api-server.md</a>). This page documents the storage contract, not the endpoints.</li><li>Talks to: <code>main.rs</code> at startup, the config HTTP route (which calls <code>VersionedConfig::update</code>), the credential refresh job (which calls <code>update_credential</code>), and every consumer via <code>VersionedConfig::get().snapshot()</code>/<code>read()</code> or <code>VersionedCache</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="sources-of-truth" tabindex="-1">Sources of truth <a class="header-anchor" href="#sources-of-truth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Sources of truth&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Authoritative schema: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/current.rs</code> (<code>Config</code>, <code>Config::check</code>, <code>Config::default</code>, <code>CONFIG_DIR</code>). Any new field belongs here plus <code>web/src/lib/types.ts</code> for the editor UI.</li><li>Authoritative defaults: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/default.rs</code> (<code>default_auth_token</code>, <code>default_bind_address</code>, <code>default_favorite_path</code>, <code>default_collection_path</code>, <code>default_submission_path</code>, <code>default_time_format</code>) and the per-type <code>Default</code> impls in <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/item.rs</code>.</li><li>Authoritative persistence: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/utils/model.rs</code> (<code>load_db_config</code>, <code>save_db_config</code>) and <code>crates/bili_sync/src/database.rs</code> (<code>database_url</code>, <code>database_connection</code>, <code>migrate_database</code>, <code>setup_database</code>).</li><li>Authoritative table shapes: the entity modules under <code>crates/bili_sync_entity/src/entities/</code> (<code>video.rs</code>, <code>page.rs</code>, <code>favorite.rs</code>, <code>collection.rs</code>, <code>submission.rs</code>, <code>watch_later.rs</code>, <code>config.rs</code>), created by <code>crates/bili_sync_migration/src/lib.rs</code>. The <code>config</code> table itself is one row with <code>id = 1</code> and the whole <code>Config</code> serialized into <code>data</code>.</li><li>Authoritative CLI/env surface: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/args.rs</code> (<code>ARGS</code>, <code>scan_only</code>, <code>log_level</code>, <code>disable_credential_refresh</code>, <code>config_dir</code>, <code>ffmpeg_path</code>).</li><li>Forbidden duplicate sources: a second config file, environment variables that duplicate config fields, per-module copies of defaults, or writing the <code>config</code> row anywhere except <code>save_db_config</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="main-paths-change-loci" tabindex="-1">Main paths / change loci <a class="header-anchor" href="#main-paths-change-loci" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Main paths / change loci&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Key entry points: <ul><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/main.rs</code> (<code>init</code>) → <code>setup_database(&amp;CONFIG_DIR.join(&quot;data.sqlite&quot;))</code> → <code>VersionedConfig::init</code>.</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/versioned_config.rs</code> (<code>VersionedConfig::{init,get,read,snapshot,subscribe,update,update_credential}</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/versioned_cache.rs</code> (<code>VersionedCache::{new,read,snapshot}</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/handlebar.rs</code> (<code>TEMPLATE: LazyLock&lt;VersionedCache&lt;Handlebars&gt;&gt;</code>).</li></ul></li><li>Common edit locations: <ul><li>Add a config field: <code>Config</code> + <code>Default</code> + <code>check</code> in <code>current.rs</code>, defaults in <code>default.rs</code>/<code>item.rs</code>, and the Svelte settings page + <code>web/src/lib/types.ts</code>.</li><li>Add a table/column: new <code>m2026…</code> module in <code>crates/bili_sync_migration/src/lib.rs</code>, entity update in <code>crates/bili_sync_entity/src/entities/</code>, then the consumers.</li><li>Change validation messages: <code>Config::check</code> (the strings are shown verbatim in the UI and tests).</li><li>Change SQLite pragmas/pool: <code>database_connection</code> in <code>database.rs</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Storage locations: <ul><li>Database: <code>CONFIG_DIR/data.sqlite</code> (WAL mode, so <code>-wal</code>/<code>-shm</code> siblings appear). <code>CONFIG_DIR</code> is <code>--config-dir</code>/<code>BILI_SYNC_CONFIG_DIR</code> or <code>dirs::config_dir()/bili-sync</code>.</li><li>Defaults for <code>upper_path</code>: <code>CONFIG_DIR/upper_face</code> (must be absolute for <code>check</code> to pass).</li><li>No other persistent file is created; QR/refresh state lives only in the <code>Config</code> row.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" tabindex="-1">Runtime paths and state transitions <a class="header-anchor" href="#runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runtime paths and state transitions&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Trigger / inputs / outputs / interfaces: <ul><li>Startup inputs: CLI args/env, then the <code>config</code> row.</li><li>Mutations: <code>PUT /api/config</code> (full <code>Config</code> JSON, validated by <code>Config::check</code> then <code>VersionedConfig::update</code>) and the credential refresh job (<code>update_credential</code>).</li><li>Outputs: <code>watch::Sender</code> notifications consumed by <code>VersionedCache</code>, which rebuilds <code>Handlebars</code> templates, the rate limiter and therefore the <code>BiliClient</code> behavior.</li></ul></li><li>Main execution path (source files and named symbols): <ol><li><code>init</code> verifies ffmpeg, calls <code>setup_database</code>, then <code>VersionedConfig::init</code>. <code>setup_database</code> creates the parent directory, runs <code>migrate_database</code>, then builds the pooled connection.</li><li><code>migrate_database</code> deliberately opens a <strong>separate default</strong> <code>Database::connect</code> for migrations (a pooled connection caused ordering issues) and first checks for the <code>m20250613_043257_add_config</code> row in <code>seaql_migrations</code>; if absent it bails with <code>该版本仅支持从 2.6.x 以上的版本升级…</code> so pre-2.6 databases are never half-migrated. Otherwise <code>Migrator::up</code> applies the migrations in <code>crates/bili_sync_migration/src/lib.rs</code>.</li><li><code>database_connection</code> sets <code>max_connections(50)</code>, <code>min_connections(5)</code>, <code>acquire_timeout(90s)</code>, <code>busy_timeout(90s)</code>, WAL journal, <code>synchronous=Normal</code>, statement logging disabled, and <code>optimize_on_close(true, None)</code>.</li><li><code>VersionedConfig::init</code> loads the row through <code>load_db_config</code>. Missing row → <code>Config::default()</code>, log <code>生成 auth_token：…，可使用该 token 登录 web UI，该信息仅在首次运行时打印</code>, then persist with <code>save_db_config</code>. A row that fails to deserialize bails <code>解析数据库配置失败： {e}</code>. The loaded <code>version</code> is reset to <code>0</code>, because it is only a concurrency token.</li><li>Each <code>VersionedConfig</code> owns <code>ArcSwap&lt;Config&gt;</code> plus a <code>watch</code> channel. <code>update</code> takes <code>update_lock</code>, rejects <code>old_config.version != new_config.version</code> with <code>配置版本不匹配，请刷新页面修改后重新提交</code>, increments the version, saves to the database <strong>before</strong> swapping the in-memory value, then publishes on the watch channel. <code>update_credential</code> does the same without the version check input (it reads the current value first).</li><li><code>VersionedCache::new(builder)</code> builds the initial value from the current config and spawns a task on the watch channel that rebuilds on every change, logging <code>Failed to update versioned cache: …</code> on failure; <code>Drop</code> cancels that task.</li></ol></li><li>State ownership, transitions and persistence: <ul><li>In-memory config is authoritative for running code; the database row is authoritative across restarts. Writes go database-first, so a failed write leaves memory unchanged.</li><li><code>version</code> is monotonic per successful update and is used only to reject stale edits. It is not persisted meaningfully across restarts (reset to 0).</li><li><code>Config::check</code> encodings: <code>upper_path</code> must be absolute; <code>video_name</code>/<code>page_name</code> non-empty; all five <code>Credential</code> fields non-empty; <code>concurrent_limit.video &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; page &gt; 0</code>; <code>Trigger::Interval</code> must be <code>&gt; 60</code> seconds; <code>Trigger::Cron</code> must parse with <code>Seconds::Required</code> and <code>dom_and_dow(true)</code>; <code>DanmakuUpdatePolicy::validate</code> requires strictly increasing milestone days and non-zero periodic interval. All errors are joined as <code>- message</code> lines.</li><li><code>Trigger</code> is <code>#[serde(untagged)]</code>: a JSON number is <code>Interval(secs)</code>, a JSON string is <code>Cron(expr)</code>; the UI therefore sends a number or a string depending on the schedule mode.</li><li><code>NFOTimeType</code> is <code>#[serde(rename_all = &quot;lowercase&quot;)]</code> → <code>favtime</code>/<code>pubtime</code>; <code>Config</code> is stored as one JSON blob, so renaming a field or enum variant breaks existing databases unless a migration rewrites the row.</li><li><code>Config</code> serializes <code>notifiers: Option&lt;Arc&lt;Vec&lt;Notifier&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> and the rest of the struct with snake_case field names (no <code>rename_all</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="organization-persistence" tabindex="-1">Organization persistence <a class="header-anchor" href="#organization-persistence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Organization persistence&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>organization_rule</code> stores each rule name, type, aggregation mode, pending aggregation target, metadata preservation flag, source and output directories. Existing rules migrate to <code>source</code>; a pending target survives interruption and blocks normal execution until retry. <code>organization_output</code> stores rule ID, video/page identity, output path and optional TV series and episode number; <code>(rule_id, bvid, cid)</code> is unique.</li><li>Deleting a rule removes its output records but leaves generated files on disk. Episode history is consequently lost; a new rule does not adopt those files. See <a href="./media-artifacts">media-artifacts.md</a> for output behavior.</li></ul><h2 id="constraints-and-failures" tabindex="-1">Constraints and failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#constraints-and-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Constraints and failures&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Invariants: <ul><li>Exactly one <code>config</code> row, <code>id = 1</code>; <code>save_db_config</code> upserts on that column.</li><li>Any config read in a long-running operation uses <code>snapshot()</code>/<code>read()</code>; never call <code>VersionedConfig::get()</code> inside a hot loop expecting fresh values per iteration.</li><li>Schema changes go through a new migration; never <code>ALTER TABLE</code> from application code.</li><li>The <code>auth_token</code> is generated once, at first run, and is never logged again. Do not add logging of it.</li></ul></li><li>Failure modes and recovery: <ul><li>Pre-2.6 database → startup error with the upgrade message (see above); there is no automatic downgrade.</li><li>Unparsable config JSON → startup fails; restore from a backup or wipe the <code>config</code> row to regenerate defaults (which generates a new <code>auth_token</code>).</li><li>Concurrent edits → second <code>PUT /api/config</code> fails with the version-mismatch message; the UI must reload.</li><li>Config validation failure → <code>update_config</code> returns the joined <code>- message</code> lines as a bad request; memory and database are untouched.</li><li><code>setup_database</code> failure surfaces as <code>数据库初始化失败</code>; permission problems on the config dir surface as <code>Failed to create config directory…</code>.</li><li>A failed <code>VersionedCache</code> rebuild only logs; the previous cached value keeps being used.</li></ul></li><li>Compatibility / migration behavior: <ul><li>Migrations in order: <code>m20240322_000001_create_table</code>, <code>m20240505_130850_add_collection</code>, <code>m20240709_130914_watch_later</code>, <code>m20240724_161008_submission</code>, <code>m20250122_062926_add_latest_row_at</code>, <code>m20250612_090826_add_enabled</code>, <code>m20250613_043257_add_config</code>, <code>m20250712_080013_add_video_created_at_index</code>, <code>m20250903_094454_add_rule_and_should_download</code>, <code>m20251009_123713_add_use_dynamic_api</code>, <code>m20260324_055217_add_staff</code>, <code>m20260712_123205_add_filter_option</code>, <code>m20260821_025000_mark_empty_tags_for_refetch</code>, <code>m20260823_000001_add_danmaku_last_synced_at</code>, <code>m20261106_000001_add_organization</code>, <code>m20261114_000001_add_aggregation_mode</code>.</li><li>New <code>Config</code> fields must have <code>#[serde(default)]</code>/defaulted types so existing rows deserialize.</li><li><code>m20260821_025000_mark_empty_tags_for_refetch</code> exists because previously stored <code>tags</code> could be empty; keep that behavior in mind when adding tag-dependent logic.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" tabindex="-1">Forbidden patterns and common mistakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Forbidden patterns and common mistakes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Forbidden: reading <code>config.json</code> or any legacy file; configuration has been database-only since 2.6.0 (<code>docs/frontend.md</code>).</li><li>Forbidden: mutating the config through <code>VersionedConfig</code> internals (for example swapping <code>inner</code>) — the watch channel would not fire and derived caches would go stale.</li><li>Forbidden: creating a <code>VersionedCache</code> per request; it spawns a task and holds a subscription.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting <code>Config::default().upper_path</code> to be relative; it is absolute inside <code>CONFIG_DIR</code>, and <code>check</code> enforces absolute.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming the version check is a lock. It is optimistic: two clients reading version <code>N</code> and both writing will have exactly one succeed.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming <code>interval</code> accepts values below the check threshold. The default is <code>1200</code> seconds; anything <code>&lt;= 60</code> fails validation, but API scans with <code>scan_only</code> do not change the schedule.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting the <code>trigger</code> semantics of a standard 5-field cron. <code>CronParser</code> requires a leading seconds field (<code>秒 分 时 日 月 周</code>), evaluated in <code>chrono::Local</code>.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting <code>config</code>-stored credentials to be encrypted. They are plain JSON — protect the database file.</li><li>Common mistake: adding a field to <code>Config</code> but not to the <code>settings</code> page; the UI submits the whole object back and would silently reset it to the default on save if the field is missing from the client model.</li></ul><h2 id="how-to-verify" tabindex="-1">How to verify <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-verify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to verify&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Startup and migration checks: <code>cargo run -- --config-dir /tmp/bili-sync-test</code> against an empty directory, then inspect <code>data.sqlite</code> (<code>sqlite3 data.sqlite &#39;select version from seaql_migrations order by version;&#39;</code> should list the registered migrations) and the single <code>config</code> row (<code>select id, length(data) from config;</code>).</li><li>Upgrade guard: copy a database without <code>m20250613_043257_add_config</code> into a fresh config dir and confirm the exact bail message instead of a partial migration.</li><li>Validation checks: <code>PUT /api/config</code> with <code>upper_path</code> relative, empty <code>video_name</code>, or <code>interval = 30</code>; each must return the corresponding Chinese message and leave the stored config unchanged.</li><li>Version check: read the config twice, update once, then replay the first body; the second call must fail with <code>配置版本不匹配…</code>.</li><li>Cache propagation: save a new <code>video_name</code> template, then trigger a scan and confirm new directories use the new template without a restart.</li><li>Existing automated checks: <code>cargo test -p bili_sync</code> (includes <code>handlebar::tests::test_template_usage</code> for <code>PathSafeTemplate</code>), <code>cargo clippy -- -D warnings</code>, <code>cargo +nightly fmt --check</code>.</li></ul>',17),a=[t];function n(s,r,l,h,u,g){return i(),o("div",null,a)}const p=e(c,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
